  "distractor_rules": {
    "roots": [
      "Keep the two bin labels fixed as adjective then adverb. Never change the words or the order.",
      "Quote exactly one target word in every stem. The quoted word is the only word to sort.",
      "Never quote a noun or a verb. Quote only the adjective or the adverb.",
      "Write one clear job for the quoted word. If a stem can be read two ways, rewrite it.",
      "Keep the pool near half adjectives and half adverbs.",
      "Tier 1 adjectives are common size, color, or feeling words next to a noun. Tier 1 adverbs are clear -ly how words.",
      "Tier 2 may use two-syllable words and when or where adverbs such as today, outside, or quietly.",
      "Tier 3 must use a word that can be both, such as fast, hard, early, late, or well, in a sentence that locks one job.",
      "Do not use pretty, very, or really as a fake adverb of degree next to another target. One quoted word only.",
      "Stem words come only from the roots wordlist, allowed_extra_words, or <NAME>. Kid world only: school, home, food, pets, play, family, weather."
    ]
  },
